# ==========================================================================
# VisioneerIT Outbound Engine — .gitignore
#
# This repo is a LOCAL backup only. It contains live campaign copy, n8n
# workflow definitions and real prospect data. Do not add a remote or push
# it anywhere without the owner's explicit decision.
# ==========================================================================

# --- SECRETS (never commit) ------------------------------------------------
# Per CLAUDE.md, secrets live in exactly two places: the n8n credential store
# and .secrets.env files on disk. Subfolders keep their own copies.
.secrets.env
*.secrets.env
**/.secrets.env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Anything whose name contains "secret", belt-and-braces. This is what keeps
#   git ls-files | grep -i secret
# empty as a zero-judgment tripwire.
*secret*
*Secret*
*SECRET*
# reach-engine/.secrets.env.example is EXCLUDED too. It was inspected and
# contains only placeholders (<your-key-here> style, no real material), so it
# is safe in principle — but it is excluded on purpose so that
#   git ls-files | grep -i secret
# stays a zero-judgment tripwire that returns nothing. If you want the
# onboarding template tracked, delete these two lines and re-add it:
#   !**/.secrets.env.example

# Service-account / private key material
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*-credentials.json
*credentials*.json
gcp-*.json
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
bower_components/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- OS / editor junk ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local tool caches / state --------------------------------------------
.gstack/
.cache/
**/.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.next/
.nuxt/
.turbo/

# --- Logs & scratch --------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
tmp/
temp/
scratch/

# --- Large binary media (regenerable; keep git usable) ---------------------
# Rendered hero videos regenerate from sendr-hero-video/<product>/index.html
# via HyperFrames. Narration mp3s regenerate from video-demo/gen-tts.sh.
# The originals stay on disk — they are simply not tracked.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi
*.mkv
*.wav
*.aiff
*.mp3
*.m4a
sendr-hero-video/*/renders/

# Per-lead scroll GIFs generated at runtime by reach-engine/make_scroll_gif.py
reach-engine/gifs/

# Small branded deliverables ARE kept (email GIFs ~450KB, posters ~32KB,
# webfonts) — they are hand-built assets referenced by the docs:
!sendr-hero-video/deliverables/*.gif
!sendr-hero-video/deliverables/*.jpg

# ARCHIVES ARE NEVER COMMITTED.
# .secrets.env is ignored above, but an archive CONTAINING one is just a binary blob to git and
# sails straight past every path rule here. oryoniq-reach-engine.zip did exactly that: it carried
# reach-engine/.secrets.env with three live production keys, plus 61 rows of prospect PII in
# leads.csv, and was committed in the very first commit (2026-08-22) — and handed to a third party
# weeks before that. Inspect any archive with `unzip -l` before it goes near this repo.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar

.claude/
